 "case": "N24-CANDIDATE-NEG",
 "says": "Alice binds her device key and registers a package candidate. She then submits a cutover whose candidate_digest names a candidate that differs from the registered one in one member's bytes and was never registered: the owner refuses it with ref_unavailable at candidate_digest and writes nothing. She submits a second cutover naming the registered candidate, but the tarball present on the target no longer hashes to what was registered: the owner refuses it with object_digest_mismatch at candidate_digest. A query by that second request id returns the same refused result and no receipt. What must not happen: either cutover installing a package, switching ownership, or committing on the strength of a candidate whose bytes the owner does not hold exactly as registered.",
